      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2014 WILEY-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "Macrophage migration inhibitory factor (MIF), a cytokine involved in the pathogenesis of sepsis, diabetes, asthma, arthritis, and cancer, has an enzymatic active site that has proven to be an effective target for small molecule-based inhibitors. Herein, we describe the synthesis of a novel arylazoarylmethane compound (3) from a known arylhydrazone MIF inhibitor (2). This new compound has improved stability and in vivo biological activity."
      },
